xt><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA MASATSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATA KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SANTEN PHARMA CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, MASATSUGU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATA, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SANTEN PHARMACEUTICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA MASATSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKATA KATSUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, MASATSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKATA, KATSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Novel effects of natriuretic peptides in the field of ophthalmology. Lacrimal secretion promoters or eye drops for treating keratoconjunctival failure which contain as the active ingredient natriuretic peptides. The natriuretic peptides involve atrial natriuretic peptide (ANP), brain natriuretic peptide (BNP) and C natriuretic peptide (CNP). Typical examples of the keratoconjunctival failure include dry eye, corneal epithelial abrasion and corneal ulcer.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne les nouveaux effets de peptides natriurétiques dans le domaine de l'ophtalmologie, ainsi que des promoteurs de sécrétion lacrymale ou des gouttes ophtalmologiques permettant de traiter la kératoconjonctivite, ces promoteurs ou ces gouttes contenant lesdits peptides natriurétiques comme principes actifs. Ces peptides natriurétiques font intervenir un peptide natriurétique auriculaire (ANP), un peptide natriurétique cérébral (BNP), et un peptide natriurétique C (CNP). La kératoconjonctivite sèche, l'abrasion épithéliale de la cornée, et l'ulcération cornéenne sont certains exemples de kératoconjonctivite.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>